# Count a connection with `totalCount`

When a selection only needs how many items a connection has, or whether it has
any, use `first: 0` and `totalCount`. Do not request `first: 1` and inspect
`edges[0].node`.

`first: 1` resolves a node and stores a partial record that a later, fuller
selection of the same id can disagree with. `totalCount` is the count the
connection already computes, and `first: 0` returns no edges.

```graphql
# Good
pendingApproval: versions(first: 0, filter: { statuses: [PENDING_APPROVAL] }) {
  totalCount
}
```

```graphql
# Bad
pendingApproval: versions(first: 1, filter: { statuses: [PENDING_APPROVAL] }) {
  edges { node { id } }
}
```

Request a real page only when the component renders fields of the node.

If another selection of the same field on that parent uses different
arguments, alias the count. Relay rejects two selections of one field with
different arguments.

See [`contrib/claude/relay.md`](../../contrib/claude/relay.md#connection-counts).
